From: MedPlatform <noreply@medplatform.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] trigger: a function handed to g_main_context_invoke returns

trigger_emit_in_main_context() was declared void and cast to GSourceFunc.
When the caller owns the main context, g_main_context_invoke() runs

    while (function (data));

so the loop ends on whatever the return register happens to hold. With no
trigger registered at all, an x86-64 build leaves zero there and returns;
an aarch64 build leaves the function's own argument, and the first
"window_focus" spins for ever at a full core, before the bar has created
its surface. The process stays alive and reports nothing.

Seen on an STM32MP257F-DK, 2026-10-12: 40 of 40 samples of the main thread
in trigger.c:86-92 and gmain.c:6533.

Upstream rewrote this function since and it returns gboolean there.

Upstream-Status: Backport [the defect is gone upstream; this is the minimal fix for v1.0_beta16]
---
diff --git a/src/trigger.c b/src/trigger.c
index c59d441..861a294 100644
--- a/src/trigger.c
+++ b/src/trigger.c
@@ -82,13 +82,15 @@ void trigger_remove ( gchar *name, GSourceFunc func, void *data )
     }
 }
 
-void trigger_emit_in_main_context ( const gchar *name )
+static gboolean trigger_emit_in_main_context ( const gchar *name )
 {
   GList *iter;
 
   if(trigger_list)
     for(iter=g_hash_table_lookup(trigger_list, name); iter; iter=iter->next)
       TRIGGER(iter->data)->func(TRIGGER(iter->data)->data);
+
+  return G_SOURCE_REMOVE;
 }
 
 void trigger_emit ( gchar *name )
